{
  "_comment": [
    "The information architecture: pillars, learning paths, and the editorial",
    "relationships between guides. Kept separate from content/articles.json so a",
    "mistake in the graph cannot break article publishing, and so the graph can be",
    "validated against the manifest rather than trusted.",
    "",
    "Every handle here must exist in content/articles.json. scripts/validate-graph.py",
    "asserts that in both directions and is part of tests/run-all.sh.",
    "",
    "An article has exactly one primary pillar (its 'up' link) and at most one",
    "learning path (its prev/next chain). It may be listed as a cluster member on",
    "other pillars — that is a reading recommendation, not a second parent.",
    "modules / labs / challenges (added 2026-09-17) are the engagement layer: a module is a Try-This generator placed in a guide (articles[].module); a lab is a controlled exercise page (pages/lab-*); a challenge is a Weekly Website Fix article in the weekly-fix blog. Cross-references are validated by scripts/validate-graph.py."
  ],
